## 2. User journeys in Chromium, 2 workers, one database per worker, login once
   concept: the setup project signs in through the UI once and saves the cookie (storageState); every journey starts signed in. Each worker clones its own database from a template and runs its own app server, and each test truncates the requests table first (no transaction: the browser's requests run on other connections). Locators are roles and labels, the way a user and a screen reader find things
   $ REPORT=reports/journeys.json npx playwright test e2e/journeys.spec.ts --output=test-results/journeys

